VALUES (
  '2026/11/26/black-friday-instalments-pay-period',
  'behaviour',
  'article',
  'Two Black Friday Instalment Plans Can Leave a $320 Pay Period',
  'Two purchases paid over four instalments, plus a previously scheduled debit, can leave a household owing $320 inside one pay period. The checkout total and the timing of the withdrawals answer different questions.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>Two different payment dates can tap the same paycheck.</strong><span> The two new purchases put $200 of debits inside the Dec. 4–17 pay period.</span></li>
<li><strong>An existing debit can lift the total to $320.</strong><span> A previously scheduled $120 charge falls in the same period as $200 of new debits.</span></li>
<li><strong>The pinch is measurable before checkout.</strong><span> A household reserving $240 per pay period would have an $80 gap in the example.</span></li>
<li><strong>Zero interest is conditional.</strong><span> The schedule assumes full and timely payment with zero fees.</span></li>
<li><strong>The same purchase total can fit differently.</strong><span> Delaying the $320 purchase past Dec. 17 would reduce the December 4–17 outflow by $80 in this illustration.</span></li>
</ul>',
  '<p>Black Friday lands on Nov. 27. A shopper who sees “four payments” twice may do the arithmetic on each purchase and still leave a hole in the household cash plan. The missing step is to lay the schedules over each other and total what falls between paydays.</p>
