VALUES (
  '2026/11/26/fhsa-december-opening-next-year-room',
  'tax',
  'article',
  'Opening an FHSA in December Can Add $8,000 of Room Next Year',
  'A first home savings account can create room before any deposit is made. Opening one before year-end also starts the account’s maximum participation period a calendar year earlier.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>The account opening is the operative event.</strong><span> An eligible first-time opener generally gets $8,000 of room in the opening year.</span></li>
<li><strong>Unused room can carry forward.</strong><span> An eligible December opener who uses none of the 2026 room can generally start 2027 with $16,000.</span></li>
<li><strong>Waiting can preserve a year at the other end.</strong><span> The 15th anniversary falls in 2041 for a 2026 opening and in 2042 for a 2027 opening.</span></li>
<li><strong>A transfer also uses participation room.</strong><span> A direct RRSP-to-FHSA transfer does not produce a new FHSA deduction.</span></li>
<li><strong>A zero deposit still means a filing step.</strong><span> CRA directs first-year openers to file Schedule 15, even without contributions or transfers.</span></li>
</ul>',
  '<p>A first-time home buyer expecting a bonus or family gift in 2027 may have a year-end decision even with no down-payment cash to invest in December. Canada Revenue Agency rules give an eligible person $8,000 in participation room in the year they open their first FHSA. The opening date therefore matters independently of the deposit date.</p>
<div class="hdq-chart">
<div style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #D0D0D0;width:100%;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
