VALUES (
  '2026/11/26/quebec-september-food-service-sales-offset',
  'economy',
  'article',
  'Quebec Erased Nearly Half of September’s Food-Service Sales Gain Elsewhere',
  'Canada’s ninth consecutive increase was smaller than the geographic moves underneath it. The provincial dollar changes show how little the national figure reveals about a local operator’s month.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>Canada’s sales rose 0.2%.</strong><span> September sales were $8.87 billion in seasonally adjusted current dollars.</span></li>
<li><strong>Quebec moved the other way.</strong><span> Its $12.18 million decline offset about 46% of the gain implied elsewhere in Canada.</span></li>
<li><strong>The biggest percentages did not drive the total.</strong><span> British Columbia added $6.47 million on 0.4% growth, nearly three times Newfoundland and Labrador’s dollar increase on 2.2% growth.</span></li>
<li><strong>The national sector mix had a drag too.</strong><span> Special food services fell $8.26 million while full-service sales rose $14.43 million.</span></li>
<li><strong>The release measures receipts.</strong><span> Use local transaction counts and average spend to diagnose what changed at a particular business.</span></li>
</ul>',
  '<p>Statistics Canada reported on Wednesday that Canadian food-service and drinking-place sales rose 0.2% in September, the ninth consecutive monthly gain. Nine provinces posted increases. The tally sounds broad, but what mattered for the size of the national move was one province going the other way.</p>
<div class="hdq-chart">
<div style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #D0D0D0;width:100%;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
<div style="background:#F9F9F9;border-bottom:1px solid #D0D0D0;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
<span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#4A5568;letter-spacing:0.02em;">How Quebec changed the national total</span>
<span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#4A5568;">−$12.18M</span>
<span style="font-size:13px;color:#4A5568;">Quebec’s contribution</span>
<span style="font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-left:auto;">CAD MILLIONS | AUG. TO SEPT. 2026</span>
</div>
<div style="padding:12px 14px 8px;">
<script>
(function(){
  var mount=document.currentScript;
  var ns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'';
  var svg=document.createElementNS(ns,''svg'');
