VALUES (
  '2026/11/26/us-thanksgiving-tsx-etf-trading-settlement',
  'market',
  'article',
  'The TSX Is Open Today. The U.S. Stocks Inside Some Canadian ETFs Are on Holiday.',
  'U.S. Thanksgiving removes one full day of regular U.S. equity trading and three hours of overlap on Friday. Canadian advisors have two distinct checks to make on orders and cash availability.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>Canadian-listed funds can keep trading.</strong><span> NYSE is closed Thursday while the Toronto exchange is open.</span></li>
<li><strong>Friday only partly restores the overlap.</strong><span> NYSE core trading ends at 1 p.m. Eastern, three hours ahead of Toronto’s normal close.</span></li>
<li><strong>A wider spread affects execution cost.</strong><span> Market makers have less direct price visibility when the underlying market is shut.</span></li>
<li><strong>A stale reference can distort comparisons.</strong><span> An ETF price may incorporate information unavailable in the last underlying closing prices.</span></li>
<li><strong>Trade and settlement calendars answer different questions.</strong><span> TMX designated Friday settlement for Wednesday’s USD-denominated trades subject to its notice.</span></li>
</ul>',
  '<p>Toronto’s equity market opens as usual on U.S. Thanksgiving. An investor can therefore buy a Canadian-listed fund that owns U.S. equities during hours when those stocks are outside their main U.S. trading session. That difference matters for anyone sending a sizable order or planning to use the proceeds of a recent sale.</p>
<div class="hdq-chart">
